    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "MIG GPT works in two stages: identifying target code snippets in the new version and migrating the out-of-tree patch. It uses a <strong>retrieval augmentation module</strong> to address structural ambiguity and missing associated fragments, a <strong>retrieval alignment module</strong> to tackle boundary indeterminacy, and a <strong>migration augmentation module</strong> to address ambiguous migration points.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flowchart illustrating the two-stage process of MIG GPT, including the three core modules and their interactions.",
